# LINE ENDINGS ARE CONTENT HERE, NOT FORMATTING.
#
# Chunking is a pure function of a document's bytes and Phase 5 shares one index
# between devices, so a fixture that arrives as CRLF on one machine and LF on
# another is not the same fixture -- it chunks differently, hashes differently,
# and the determinism test fails for a reason that has nothing to do with the
# chunker. Git's autocrlf would do exactly that, silently, on a Windows
# checkout.
#
# So: no translation, anywhere, for anything.
* -text

# The chunking fixtures are the case this file exists for. One of them contains
# deliberate CRLF line endings BECAUSE that is a real thing to find in a vault,
# and it must survive a round trip through a clone.
test/fixtures/** -text -diff
